{
  "$comment": [
    "The Unreal block publishes its own copy of the road centrelines (`hosts.unreal.road_splines`, MPB 1.16.0;",
    "a 2.0 bundle names its `-Engine` twin there too), and a reader prefers it to the shared layer (HPS-52).",
    "",
    "Why it exists: the Unreal host is fixed-frame vertically, its landscape EGM2008 orthometric on every",
    "order, and from 1.8.0 a US order's shared `road_splines` layer is NAVD88 (GEOID18), which",
    "`manifest.roadSplinesStatedDatum` refuses by name. The copy is the same roads draped on the engine's",
    "ground, so its heights are the landscape's and are placed as the file carries them. Nothing here",
    "converts a height: the published offset between the datums is one number for the whole site and is",
    "not this host's to apply, so a layer in the wrong datum is never shifted, only refused or passed over.",
    "",
    "A reader tries the sources in order -- the copy, then the shared layer -- and places the first it can",
    "read whose datum is its own. The datum of each is asked of what it states, never assumed from the",
    "pointer's name: a copy stating anything but `EGM2008-orthometric` verbatim (NAVD88, a datum no reader",
    "knows, a spelling that differs only in case, or none at all) is refused by name and the shared layer",
    "is judged on its own datum as before. A US order whose manifest publishes no copy (1.8.0 to 1.15.0, or",
    "a US order whose engine DEM was not staged) places no road, as `manifest.roadSplinesStatedDatum` has it,",
    "and an order outside the US, or a bundle from before 1.8.0, places the shared layer exactly as before.",
    "",
    "`manifest` is one embedded 1.16.0 US document. Each row lays its own members over it before it is",
    "parsed -- `root` over the document, `unreal` over `hosts.unreal`, `engineRoadSplines` over",
    "`hosts.unreal.road_splines` and `roadSplines` over the `road_splines` entry of `vector.layers`; a",
    "value sets a member and null removes it -- so the decision is proven through the parser, not beside",
    "it. A row's `declared` lists the sources the manifest names, in the order they are tried, and",
    "`placeable` the ones among them whose heights may be placed, in that order: the first is the one the",
    "roads are read from. `errorContains` is asserted against the refusals of the sources that are not",
    "placeable, and `enginePath` against the path the copy is read from."
  ],
